  "term": "impingement",
  "definition": "In this packet, impingement refers to a painful hand problem affecting a finger or thumb when a flexor tendon is mechanically caught as it passes through a narrowed pulley near the metacarpal head. This can lead to thickening of the tendon sheath and sometimes nodule formation.",
